<h2>Cold check &mdash; one row per tool</h2>

<p>
  Each tool checks the same corpus: <strong>{{ benchmarks.rows.length }}</strong> fixtures, each a large
  (2k&ndash;4k line) Python file stressing one typing-spec construct &mdash; TypedDicts, overloads,
  protocols, narrowing, and so on. The number that honestly summarises a tool is the
  <strong>distribution of its cold check across that corpus</strong>: its median, and the fixtures at
  each end of its own range. <em>Reports diagnostics on</em> shows how many fixtures the tool actually
  flagged in the measured configuration &mdash; checkers differ in what they implement, and a fast time
  on a file a tool diagnoses nothing in means less than the same time with findings.
</p>

